      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did this to minimize the performance impact. I think it\u0027d simplify things greatly to *always* copy. I\u0027d like to do that in a follow on CL (and get rid of the new private method on SkPixmap) in order to separate that broader perf impact from this bug fix.\n\nPreviously I was attempting to make GPU use a SkImage_Raster\u0027s SkMipmap\u0027s contents when making a cached texture version of the image rather than repopulating the levels on the GPU (skbug.com/11983). However, I ran into difficulty because the cached texture uses the bitmap\u0027s generation ID in its cache key. However, this method allows two SkImage_Raster\u0027s to have SkBitmaps with the same ID but with different SkMipmaps. I think always copying and thus creating a new ID is the way forward.\n\nLonger term I think SkBitmap should work like textures: either it has mips or it doesn\u0027t and perhaps SkMipmaps move to SkPixelRef. The current late attachment is too disconnected from the rest of the SkPixelRef state (gen id, immutability, etc). But this is probably easier when we get further along with making images either be mipped or and away from making cached SkMipmaps.",
